## 6. Source-integrity problems

1. **Footnote [^1] "more than 5 million square feet"**: Previously tagged `[VERIFY: sq-ft vs. July 29, 2026 release]`. Confirmed from the primary PR Newswire release and MWAA press release. Tag removed; claim confirmed.

2. **Footnote [^16] date**: "February 2026" referred to the reissued report date (February 25, 2026); the NTSB board voted and initially published on January 27, 2026. Corrected to reflect both dates.

3. **Footnote [^16] probable cause**: Draft assigned cause only to the FAA. NTSB found multiple contributing parties. Corrected to list all four causal elements.

4. **Footnote [^17] $235.8M grants**: Figure appears in the MWAA context packet (not a primary source per the evidence map warning). Public reporting identifies $187.4M from ATP grants. Footnote updated to note the discrepancy and qualify the figure as "per MWAA program documentation."

5. **E-0070 Port Authority hearing loop**: Evidence record notes "Trade-press description; primary PANYNJ standard document not opened." Independent web search confirmed the October 2020 PANYNJ manual and hearing loop mandate from multiple accessibility advocacy sources. Claim upgraded from qualified to verified.

6. **SFO "United-anchored pilot"**: Not explicitly in the evidence record but confirmed from Airport Industry Review (Dec 2020): "United Airlines served as the primary test carrier." Confirmed ✓.

